Now, that I know what actually happened on the planes, they all where
pretty useless, particularly cold and missile. I'm used to play wizards
before, but cone of cold and magic missile from a high level wizard's book
spell are something entirely different than the poor magic from the wands.

The background for the 2 /WoCM where some reminiscence of spoilers or
postings (I must have got them wrong), where a player created a horde of
bugs or ants to build some kind of barrier against the raiders. Besides
the fact that it never could work with an uncontrolled CM, there was just
no place on astral for creating *anything* around me and thus I didn't
even try. Just a silly waste of weight capacity...

The /WoPoly was something special to me: Got the wand very late in the
game (on the 'home run') and finally was able to polypile 2(!) magic
whistles, which I never found in the game before but which where nearly
useless now. Those missing magic whistles where the main reason for going
petless in the late game, what was new for me.
Nevertheless, the whistle made it possible to ascend together with my
guardian angel, which often was seperated from me and surely would have
died w/o whistling her out of the trouble occasionally. I still think that
was worth the drop of polyless conduct.

At least in the end game I was thinking lawful! ;-)


